      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-122",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CWE-122 - Heap-based Buffer Overflow\nVulnerability: Heap buffer overflow in itoa due to insufficient buffer allocation\nDescription: A heap-based buffer overflow vulnerability exists in the itoa() function due to \ninsufficient buffer allocation in the bad1() function. The vulnerability occurs when \nthe docWidth variable, parsed from user-controlled input, is used to determine the \nsize of a heap buffer allocated via malloc(). When a small value (e.g., 1 byte) is \nallocated but itoa() attempts to convert a large integer like INT_MAX (2147483647), \nwhich requires 11 bytes including the null terminator, the function writes beyond \nthe allocated buffer boundary. This results in a heap buffer overflow that can \ncorrupt adjacent heap structures, potentially leading to arbitrary code execution \nor denial of service.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "cp-user-itoa/mock_vp.c"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 24,
                  "endLine": 24,
                  "startColumn": 14,
                  "endColumn": 14
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
